#: processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The entry point is an INTENT TO EDIT, not a request to copy. Drawing it this way is deliberate: a reader does not set out to make a copy, they set out to change something, and the copy is what the rule turns that into. A diagram starting at \"copy this\" would never be reached by the person who needs it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn:77
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The one gate. `check:read-only-graphs` answers it from the directory's declaration, and `readOnly` absent is NOT `false` — it is not declared, a third state. An undeclared directory holding materialized nodes is reported as a finding rather than waved through here, because \"nobody answered\" and \"somebody said it is writable\" must not share a branch."
msgstr ""

#: processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The ordinary path, drawn so the process does not read as though every edit needs a copy. Content in a writable directory is authored content and is edited where it lives; the copy-out is for somebody else's bytes, not for yours."
msgstr ""

#: processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn:115
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The step that is easy to omit and impossible to reconstruct afterwards. `provenance` is a PAIR: `upstream` is the remote thing, `local` is the original in this repository. A copy-out writes `local`; it does not overwrite `upstream`, and it does not reuse `upstream` for a local value — that was one field until 2026-09-22, and by then 5 of the 9 who-iris item records were using it for a local one in violation of its own documentation. Without `local`, one rename later the copy is indistinguishable from original work and nothing downstream can repair it, because the information was never written down."
msgstr ""

#: processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "This lane holds exactly one task and it WRITES NOTHING, which is the point of drawing it at all. A lane that is only ever read from is the visible form of the rule: the arrow runs out of here and never back. Task_ReadSource is where the process would go wrong if anybody added a step, so its emptiness is load-bearing rather than incidental."
msgstr ""

#: processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn:62
#. Diagram label
msgid "Verification"
msgstr ""

#: processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn:124
#. Diagram label
msgid "Verify the ORIGINAL still hashes to its digest"
msgstr ""

#: processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Where the copy lands, chosen by the owner 2026-09-22 over a scratch area. A scratch area lost because it makes the copy publishable by accident: a directory nobody declared is a directory nobody gates. The two writes here are ordered and both required — Task_Land puts the bytes somewhere, Task_RecordProvenance says what they are a copy OF, and a process that stopped after the first would produce a file indistinguishable from original work one rename later."
msgstr ""

